WEBVTT

00:13:58.072 --> 00:14:00.479
and he said, "We're selling culture."

00:14:01.255 --> 00:14:05.320
And you know, my reaction,
as an organizational psychologist was,

00:14:05.344 --> 00:14:07.804
"I'm pretty sure you're
leasing buildings."

00:14:08.523 --> 00:14:10.236
It seemed like there was a big,

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:14.318
you know, a little bit of a leap
from what the actual work was

00:14:14.342 --> 00:14:16.176
to the mission that it was serving,

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:19.759
and of course, sometimes
those leaps are aspirational.

00:14:19.783 --> 00:14:22.634
Sometimes they're part of creating

00:14:22.658 --> 00:14:24.699
a meaningful and compelling vision.

00:14:24.723 --> 00:14:28.350
But the disconnect felt
a little bit more significant to me

00:14:28.374 --> 00:14:30.592
than I see in a lot of workplaces.